# wbic16-boardy.phext
The shape of one man's Twitter graph and his interactions across it, built as a worked example in Boardy's methodology (spec and boot manual, wbic16/boardy-tools, 2026-11-18). One search, mapped: SELF spanned a social graph for 17 years looking for minds who could see what he was building. This artifact encodes that graph's shape in Boardy's nine node kinds and fourteen edge types, at full-archive scale, and closes with a counterfactual verdict on whether the method would have run the search faster.

Sources: SELF's Twitter archive snapshot ending 2025-06-16 (29,539 tweets; follower and following lists; 47,973 like records; DM headers, metadata only), plus SELF's people-file records through 2026-11-18 for post-archive beats. The archive holds SELF's side only; every other person's own posts are absent from it.

Alias policy (absolute): no names, no handles, no identifying details appear in this file. Persons are aliases: SELF (the searcher, the archive's owner) and M01-M25 (mutuals, assigned by archive reply rank, then structural cases). Everyone else appears only as aggregate classes (T-scrolls, Volume 3 Book 3). The alias key is a separate private file and is not part of this artifact. Rationale, in Boardy's own discipline: these people never agreed to be evidence; the artifact carries shape only.

Two layers, kept apart:
- Record layer: scrolls carry the temporal approach data (counts, dates, shapes). This is content, not structure.
- Graph layer: nodes and typed weighted edges in Boardy's schema only, built strictly from the record. Where the record cannot support an edge, the family stays empty and the gap is logged in Volume 5. Nothing is fabricated across an empty family.

Coordinate map:
- Volume 1: front matter (this header; the signal-to-edge mapping; the full-archive accounting; the temporal shape of the whole search).
- Volume 2: problem space - asks A1-A5 and blocker B1.
- Volume 3: solution space. Book 1: nodes (SELF; M01-M25; works W1-W4; channels CH1-CH4; claims C1-C3; metric MT1; events EV1-EV4). Book 2: temporal records at the same scroll numbers as Book 1's person scrolls. Book 3: tail classes T1-T7.
- Volume 4: the join. Book 1: edges E01-E26. Book 2: candidate joins CJ1-CJ6 the layout surfaces.
- Volume 5: the gap log, G1-G12.
- Volume 6: the counterfactual verdict (analysis, labelled as such).

Totals: 48 graph nodes (26 person, 5 ask, 1 blocker, 4 work, 4 channel, 3 claim, 1 metric, 4 event, 0 org); 26 typed edges, total weight 55, of which 12 edges are in his five dense families (weakens holds none). Behind the graph layer, the record layer accounts for the whole archive: 7,680 distinct handles in the tweet record, 897 mutual-follow accounts, 369 DM partners. 134 scrolls.
# Signal-to-edge mapping
How each archive signal was treated, stated before the fact, per the build brief. Boardy's edge catalogue has fourteen types; his five person-involving families include one - person->person - that is empty on purpose. Most of what a Twitter archive measures lives in exactly that family.

- replies (17,495) -> NO EDGE. person->person is empty by his law. Carried as temporal records (Volume 3 Book 2) and class aggregates. Defense: the archive's loudest signal is the one his schema refuses to store; storing it anyway would fail his Invention axis on the first edge.
- mentions (14,668) -> NO EDGE. Same family, same treatment.
- retweets of a person by SELF (4,414) -> NO EDGE. Amplification is still person->person. Carried as counts in temporal records. One exception in kind, not in signal: a mutual amplifying SELF's central claim in their own voice is an assertion, and is edged as asserts (E08) on the strength of SELF's 2026-11-11 core analysis, not of the retweet count.
- likes (47,973) -> NO EDGE and NO TARGET. The archive's like records carry no author field (URLs are in /i/web/ form), so the channel's reach cannot be enumerated from this data. Logged as gap G9; no external resolution attempted.
- follow / mutual-follow status -> NO EDGE. A node-level fact recorded in person scrolls ("mutual: yes/no at snapshot"). The follow graph (1,773 followers / 1,699 following / 897 mutual) is population, not ties.
- DM existence and volume -> NO per-person edge. SELF reaches the graph through the DM channel (E21, reaches_via). Per-person message counts (metadata only; no content read) live in temporal records.
- a stated ask in the record -> ask node + needs edge, weight 2 (his reference instance's calibration for needs). Five such asks exist in the whole record.
- a shipped thing in the record -> work node + made edge, weight 3 for a person's central work, 2 for secondary works.
- a stated position in the record -> claim node + asserts edge: weight 3 for SELF's central claims, 2 for a position stated once or held by another person.
- a work visibly carrying a claim -> supports edge, weight 2-3.
- a platform removing a relied-upon tool -> blocker node (kind: technical, the only enum kind that fits a platform-side removal) + blocked_by edge, weight 3.
- a dated recognition or disclosure event -> event node + evidences edge, weight 1-2.
- a directory a person operates -> work node; would_fill edge at weight 1 toward the standing ask, labelled weak and partial in its scroll.
- a stated position against the central claim -> contradicts edge, weight 2.
- a computed re-measurement of a work -> metric node + measures edge, weight 2.
- SELF's contact with the whole graph -> reaches_via edges to four channel nodes, weights 3/2/1/2 by what each channel demonstrably carried: replies carried the search; mentions were secondary; likes are signal without text; DM was real but private and late (93% of its volume is 2023 or later).

Signals with no home in the schema were not forced into one. They are in the gap log (Volume 5), which is part of the deliverable, not an appendix of failures.
# Full-archive accounting
Every number below is computed from the archive snapshot ending 2025-06-16. The node and signal totals cover the whole archive, not the aliased subset.

Population:
- tweets by SELF: 29,539 (2008 to 2025-06-16)
- followers: 1,773 accounts; following: 1,699; mutual (both directions): 897
- distinct handles appearing in the tweet record: 7,680 (4,164 reply targets; 4,948 mention targets; 2,010 retweeted authors; the sets overlap)
- of the 897 mutual accounts, 478 resolve to a handle in the interaction record; 419 (46.7%) show zero interaction of any kind in the archive and no handle is recoverable for them from it
- DM partners: 369 (117 resolve to handles in the tweet record; 252 are ID-only)

Signals (all SELF's, outbound - the archive holds no one else's posts):
- replies: 17,495 (59.2% of all tweets)
- mention instances outside reply targets: 14,668
- retweets: 4,414
- likes: 47,973 (no dates, no authors - see gap G9)
- DM messages: 6,077 across 369 conversations (metadata only)

Where the replies went:
- to mutuals: 5,854 (33.5%)
- to non-mutual targets: 11,641 (66.5%), across 3,719 accounts; excluding SELF's own account (1,008 self-replies, thread continuations), the two largest one-directional targets absorbed 348 and 266 replies - more than any mutual received
- the aliased top 20 mutuals hold 2,204 replies (12.6% of all replies); 165 accounts of all kinds hold 50%
- reply-target distribution (4,164 accounts): exactly 1 reply: 2,572 (61.8%); 2-4: 996; 5-9: 305; 10-49: 237; 50-99: 40; 100+: 14
- mutual handles by reply band (478): 100+: 10; 50-99: 22; 10-49: 96; 5-9: 74; 2-4: 128; exactly 1: 115; zero replies (mention/retweet traces only): 33
# Temporal shape of the whole search
The approach, at archive scale. Replies by SELF per year, with the phase each year belongs to:

2008: 0 replies (6 tweets) - the account exists; nothing yet
2009: 17 - first traces
2010: 5
2011: 16
2012: 259 - first build begins (1,360 tweets)
2013: 740
2014: 962
2015: 1,398 - first-era peak; the word for the exocortex is coined in conversation this year (with M01)
2016: 798
2017: 469 - the sag
2018: 295 - quietest year of the middle period; the DM channel carries exactly 1 message
2019: 722
2020: 855
2021: 633
2022: 372 - the quiet year that ends with the artifact: the format's first commit lands 2022-11-29, after only 607 tweets all year
2023: 1,582 - the naming (2023-11-12/13) and the surge: 481 new reply targets; the founding cluster arrives within weeks
2024: 7,096 - the flood: 10,973 tweets (37.1% of the archive), 1,102 new reply targets, 1,384 active targets, 3,630 DM messages
2025: 1,276 (to June 16, where the snapshot ends)

New reply targets per year tell the same story from the other side: the search met 368 new accounts in 2015, 481 in 2023, 1,102 in 2024 - and 99 in 2022, the year the thing being searched with was actually built. The spanning was widest exactly when there was least to show, and the population the search was for arrived only after the artifact existed (see Volume 6).
node: A1
kind: ask
purpose: find the minds who can see the format - recognition of what the exocortex and its text format are, one mind at a time
granularity: a person
urgency: standing - open since the search began (2008), still open
held by: SELF (edge E13)
blocked_by: none stated. The obstruction on this ask fits none of the spec's four blocker kinds; no edge was fabricated. See gap G6 - the absence is one of this artifact's findings.
node: A2
kind: ask
purpose: a quest - a publicly expressed need for an undertaking, stated by M12 in November 2026
granularity: one undertaking
urgency: open (no date stated)
held by: M12 (edge E14)
note: post-archive record (SELF's people files, 2026-11-07). SELF's response - a quest-framed claim of an exocortex - was drafted the same day; sending is SELF's act. This is the one ask in the graph currently being worked as a join (CJ6).
node: A3
kind: ask
purpose: a voice mode as good as the one being retired, for hours-long voice-first work (mapping undocumented processes by talking)
granularity: a working tool, in the form the work requires
urgency: hard deadline - the incumbent tool is retired 2026-12-11
held by: M24 (edge E15)
blocked_by: B1 (edge E12)
note: post-archive record (2026-11-14). The most completely specified ask in the entire graph: purpose, granularity, and urgency all stated by the asker herself. SELF answered it by hand the day it appeared (CJ4).
node: A4
kind: ask
purpose: what teaming up would take - M21's question on SELF's long-arc story project (spanning 2033-2130), asked 2026-11-05
granularity: a collaboration
urgency: open
held by: M21 (edge E16)
note: post-archive record. The asker initiated contact himself after years of zero-signal mutual following (see M21's temporal record). SELF's answer: step 1 is internalizing the problems the format solves.
node: A5
kind: ask
purpose: a speaker on the table that passively listens to a group and captures what matters (M23's product request, posted March 2024)
granularity: a product
urgency: unstated by the asker - and it waited 20 months (see CJ3)
held by: M23 (edge E17)
note: SELF saw the ask when it was posted and routed it to his own project account to capture the idea. No report back to the asker is in the record until drafts were prepared in November 2026.
node: B1
kind: blocker
blocker kind: technical
note: the platform retires the voice mode M24's work relies on, on a fixed date (2026-12-11). Alternatives exist; none matches the form the work requires (record, 2026-11-14). Nothing in the record weakens this blocker; SELF's answer routed around it through his own knowledge, delivered by hand - the manual's legitimate routing, not an edge (see gap G7).
