class: T1 - mutuals below the aliased line (known handles)
The 478 mutual accounts whose handles the interaction record recovers, by replies received: 100+: 10 accounts; 50-99: 22; 10-49: 96; 5-9: 74; 2-4: 128; exactly 1: 115; zero replies (mention or retweet traces only): 33.
The aliased M01-M20 are drawn from the top of this class. The 96 accounts at 10-49 replies are the graph's middle: real, sustained, and entirely without recorded asks or offers - the record holds their counts and nothing the join could match on.
class: T2 - one-directional targets (the penumbra)
3,719 accounts received replies without being mutuals; they absorbed 11,641 replies - 66.5% of all replies SELF ever sent, twice what the entire mutual graph received.
Excluding SELF's own account (1,008 self-replies, thread continuations), the largest targets absorbed 348 and 266 replies each - more than any mutual ever received (the top mutual holds 188) - with no follow-back recorded at snapshot. The record names this pattern itself: a one-directional penumbra around a mutual core.
Boardy's method has no representation for this class at all: they are not in a consenting graph, they stated no asks, and person->person is empty. Two-thirds of the search's energy landed in a class his schema cannot hold. (Volume 6 returns to this.)
class: T3 - the one-reply breadth
2,572 accounts (61.8% of all reply targets) received exactly one reply from SELF, ever. Another 996 received 2-4.
This is the spanning made visible: for seventeen years the search touched thousands of minds once and moved on. Any one of them could have been M06. Nothing in a single reply distinguishes the one who would have understood from the 2,571 who did not - the distinguishing event only exists at second contact, and for this class there was no second contact.
class: T4 - mention-only and retweet-only accounts
3,473 handles appear only as mentions (never replied to); 43 more appear only as authors SELF retweeted. Total distinct handles in the tweet record: 7,680.
These are the graph's peripheral vision: named, pointed at, never conversed with. In Boardy's schema they are not nodes - no intake ever occurred. In the search's reality they are the visible horizon the spanning moved through.
class: T5 - DM partners
369 conversation partners, 6,077 messages (metadata only in this artifact; content was not read). 117 partners resolve to handles in the tweet record; 252 are ID-only and cannot be aliased from this data.
The largest private channel (613 messages) belongs to an account ranked 21st by replies - just below the aliased line. Among aliased persons the DM-heavy relationships are M15 (289), M06 (284), M03 (234), M25 (99), M05 (53), M14 (47).
By year the channel is an artifact-era phenomenon: 2012-2022 combined carry 403 messages; 2023 carries 739; 2024 carries 3,630.
class: T6 - follow-graph only
Beyond the 897 mutuals: 876 accounts follow SELF without being followed back, and 802 are followed by SELF without following back (at snapshot). Most never interact with SELF in the archive at all.
They are population, not graph: no signals, no intake, no edges. Boardy's method would not count them as nodes. The search counted them as territory.
class: T7 - the silent mutuals
419 of the 897 mutual accounts (46.7%) show zero interaction of any kind in the entire archive - no reply, mention, retweet, or like trace - and no handle is recoverable for them from the archive.
Two aliased persons come from this class's edge (M21, M24), and both became structurally important only through post-archive events: one activated himself with an explicit ask; the other posted the best-specified ask in the graph. The other 417 are indistinguishable from them in the data. Any of them could be carrying an A3. The archive cannot say, and this artifact does not guess.
